<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Jabal Druze State</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – 1936 CE · capital Suwayda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A French-created autonomous state for the Druze of the Hawran mountains, where the Great Syrian Revolt of 1925 began.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1921 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> reached an agreement with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> leaders granting the mountainous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabal-al-druze">Jabal al-Druze</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, autonomy under French protection. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salim-al-atrash">Salim al-Atrash</a>, of the leading Druze family, became its first governor.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> customary leadership, with French advisers. After Salim's death in 1923, the French officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriel-carbillet">Gabriel Carbillet</a> governed it, imposing roads and land reforms with forced labour and challenging the power of the Atrash chiefs. Druze anger led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-al-atrash">Sultan al-Atrash</a> to rise in July 1925, defeating French columns and sparking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-syrian-revolt">Great Syrian Revolt</a>, which spread to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> before it was crushed in 1927.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The state was renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabal-al-druze">Jabal al-Arab</a>, and under the 1936 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-syrian-treaty-of-independence">Franco-Syrian treaty</a> it was joined to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-republic">Syrian Republic</a>, becoming the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suwayda">Suwayda</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jabal-druze-state.jpg" alt="Jabal Druze State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jabal_ad-Druze_(state).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – 1936 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Suwayda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Salim al-Atrash, Gabriel Carbillet</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Druze</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Syria</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>State of Jabal al-Druze, Jabal al-Arab</dd></dl></aside></div>
